Z||000000||AL||06-25-2001||01:33 AM||||<BR>how do i hook up a amp to power 2 more speakers?and if i do that can my stock amp still work to power my speakers in the front and back and my sub? or do i have to power everything with my new amp?<BR>thanks<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=522257&a=3823750&p=50501513&Sequence=1&res=high">  <BR>84 Indy 4 speed<BR>86gt<BR>89 gta<P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||06-25-2001||03:29 AM||||That all depends on what size your amp is... you dont want to run 2 subs and speakers off a 200 watt amp... its not enough power... Plus its not suggested on most amps because the crossover (if it even has a built in one) wont be set for sub output if you want to hear the highs, or you wont hear highs if its set to heat loud bass!  Best way is run a 4 or 2 channel highs amp and a sub amp (depending on how many speakers you have)..  Bridge the sub amp for more power!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
